WEBVTT

00:16:28.458 --> 00:16:30.893
excited about the deal.

00:16:30.917 --> 00:16:32.684
AG: That's kind of shocking to hear.

00:16:32.708 --> 00:16:35.809
You had a deal in place, you slept on it,

00:16:35.833 --> 00:16:37.476
and then you said, "You know what?

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.476
I'm gonna make another concession,
even though I don't need to.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:43.309
JB: And I think it helped
our relationship with the player.

00:16:43.333 --> 00:16:46.048
In future negotiations with him,
he was very open with me.

00:16:46.072 --> 00:16:48.506
He was very to the point
on what he was looking for.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:51.559
I was very to the point,
and most of our conversations

00:16:51.583 --> 00:16:54.393
and negotiations moved on
very smoothly from there.

00:16:54.417 --> 00:16:56.417
AG: The lesson was that even if he managed

00:16:56.441 --> 00:16:58.226
to win this one negotiation,

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.059
it might have unintended consequences